{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-28T14:08:32.363Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"39f0409326ff3a93bdf4de17","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"argv"},"topic":null,"version":{"value":"2.1.332","source":"probe"}},"op":"create","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/id","value":"pm-kxmu54"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/title","value":"The release Sentry gate blocks on a resolved issue that regressed only through environment=test events, because it judges test traffic per issue instead of per regression"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/description","value":"Observed 2026-11-28. Blocker #1794's blocker_retry run 46149734279 failed at the sentry-telemetry-gate on PM-CLI-42. The issue had been resolved at 13:25Z after its two automation events (11-26, 11-27) were explained. At 13:39Z, four new events from a pm-github reproduction harness arrived correctly labelled environment=test, and they regressed it. pm-usn5k2 made the gate drop an unresolved issue only when a complete listing of issues with any non-test event (!environment:test !pm.source_context:test, at any time) lacks it. PM-CLI-42 still has its old automation events, so its test-only regression counts as release-blocking. Today's retry marker was then spent, so the day's release needed an operator dispatch and a time-boxed archive. Expected: a regression is judged by the events since the issue was last resolved. When every event after the last resolution is test traffic (environment test or pm.source_context test), the issue is test-only for the gate. An issue never resolved, a regression with any non-test event, or a lookup that fails or is incomplete keeps blocking (fail closed). Duplicate check: searched 'sentry gate test-only regression resolved issue environment test events'. pm-usn5k2 (closed) owns the per-issue test-only rule, and no item owns post-resolution judgement."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/type","value":"Issue"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/status","value":"open"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/priority","value":1},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/tags","value":["auto-release","gate","release","sentry","telemetry","test-isolation"]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/created_at","value":"2026-11-28T14:08:32.363Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-28T14:08:32.363Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/author","value":"harness:claude-code"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/estimated_minutes","value":90},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/acceptance_criteria","value":"An unresolved issue whose events since its last resolution are all environment=test or pm.source_context=test is reported as test-only and does not block; A never-resolved issue, a regression with any non-test event since the resolution, and a failed or truncated activity or event lookup keep blocking; The gate spec covers each case with mocked Sentry responses, and a live gate run reports the classification"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/parent","value":"pm-5oj5"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/risk","value":"medium"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/confidence","value":80},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/severity","value":"high"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/expected_result","value":"A resolved issue that regresses only through test events no longer blocks the daily release, while any non-test regression still does"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/dependencies","value":[{"id":"pm-usn5k2","kind":"discovered_from","created_at":"2026-11-28T14:08:32.363Z","author":"harness:claude-code","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"}]}],"before_hash":"3cc22dff72be7b14824654a7a64ea62b04799939b2fee54c1b5f52ca60bf6df0","after_hash":"a39395db5e87a8b0fd5771b628ab89bc6a9635bff5fabfc55819309b119c7959","item_hash_version":3,"mess